        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-28T14:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally speaking an unqualified method sounds to me like it take everything into account, so \"isUidNetworkingBlocked\" sounds to me like it will return true if a lockdown VPN is blocking this UID. It may also be useful to keep a method that will actually return the full thing. It would be useful at least in l.7524, and if we\u0027re willing to give up the optimizations, it would be useful in other places below too.\n\nBarring that, I think we should rename it to something that makes clear it doesn\u0027t account for VPN. Or, we could replace this method with a static import of NPMI.isUidNetworkingBlocked, or inline it, but NPMI will have to go soon for mainline so that\u0027s a less attractive option.\n\nA last option would be to have an optimized method returning both booleans (say in an int) for both old and new versions to avoid copying the code in l.7562 and 7584.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2026,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2026,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "83789533f8d5f8362922f7f9909779231adcf1e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a63341f7_8bf0079f",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 2026,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-30T16:58:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Renamed to isUidBlockedByRules for now.\n\nI could leave as isUidNetworkingBlocked, and simply add a \"boolean isBlockedByVpn\" which the caller would have to calculate (using isUidBlockedByVpn) and pass in. Would that be better?\n\nI\u0027m not sure it\u0027s worth giving up the performance improvements to have a single method. That\u0027s because in many cases, when we call this method, we do so twice, once with old inputs, and once with new inputs have changed and we need to re-evaluate.\n\nBut that said... currently, the set of blocked UIDs is pretty much always \"a full UID range with one hole, for every userId that has lockdown enabled\". That means usually 0 elements, sometimes 3 elements (one always-on VPN), rarely 6 elements (always-on VPN in both primary profile and work profile). So maybe the performance actually doesn\u0027t matter.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "7977604b_89b3b81f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2026,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2026,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "83789533f8d5f8362922f7f9909779231adcf1e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
