        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-28T14:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this in fact be a list ?\nRationale : multiple VPNs for different users in lockdown mode are handled in different VPN objects and each handling their list of UIDs. Hopefully there should be no overlap, but if two of them happen to have the same UID range somewhere, the first to remove this range will unblock the range, while the other VPN still expects it blocked.\n\nHow does netd behave if the same range is added twice ? Will it add an identical set of rules, or deduplicate ? If the former, then a list is surely the right thing to do, seeing as we never diff and simply pass on to netd exactly what was sent to setRequireVpnForUids. If not then the set is better as it will correctly represent what netd really has.\n\nAlternatively we could imagine some way to forbid overlaps, but that would require some concept of ownership of range per-VPN which is pretty annoying to implement.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5967,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 5967,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "83789533f8d5f8362922f7f9909779231adcf1e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
